('127.247.d.4.H',4,'Professional development benefits a company by:','["Lowering morale", "Improving employee skills and retention", "Reducing quality", "Increasing turnover"]'::jsonb,1,'Growth keeps talent.','original'),
('127.247.d.4.I',3,'To attract top workers, a company may offer pay, benefits, and:','["Fewer duties", "No schedule", "Competitive compensation", "Closed doors"]'::jsonb,2,'Compensation must be competitive.','original'),
('127.247.d.4.I',4,'Employee compensation includes wages and:','["Nothing else", "Free parking only", "Office supplies", "Benefits such as health insurance"]'::jsonb,3,'Benefits are part of compensation.','original'),
('127.247.d.4.J',3,'Reducing the number of employees to cut costs is:','["Downsizing", "Hiring", "Promoting", "Expanding"]'::jsonb,0,'Downsizing reduces headcount.','original'),
('127.247.d.4.J',4,'A company might consider downsizing when:','["Demand rises", "Sales drop sharply and costs must fall", "It is hiring", "Profits soar"]'::jsonb,1,'Downsizing responds to weak results.','original'),
('127.247.d.4.K',3,'When many employees quit, a company faces high:','["Savings", "Profit", "Turnover costs", "Growth"]'::jsonb,2,'Turnover is expensive.','original'),
('127.247.d.4.K',4,'One way to reduce turnover is to:','["Remove training", "Ignore complaints", "Cut raises", "Improve pay, recognition, and working conditions"]'::jsonb,3,'Satisfied employees stay.','original'),
('127.247.d.4.L',3,'A workforce with people of different backgrounds can bring:','["A wider range of ideas and perspectives", "Less creativity", "Higher conflict only", "Fewer skills"]'::jsonb,0,'Diversity broadens thinking.','original'),
('127.247.d.4.L',4,'A benefit of a diverse workforce is that it:','["Excludes talent", "Reflects and understands diverse customers", "Limits growth", "Reduces ideas"]'::jsonb,1,'Diversity helps serve markets.','original'),
('127.247.d.4.M',3,'Researching a company''s recent layoffs and how it managed them is:','["Hiring", "Training", "Studying a contemporary HR case", "Advertising"]'::jsonb,2,'Case research builds insight.','original'),
('127.247.d.4.M',4,'When researching a diversity case, a student should:','["Guess", "Use rumors", "Copy a classmate", "Use credible news and company reports"]'::jsonb,3,'Reliable sources are key.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.A',3,'An inner drive that pushes people to act to reach a goal is:','["Motivation", "Delay", "Fatigue", "Confusion"]'::jsonb,0,'Motivation drives behavior.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.A',4,'A manager who understands what drives employees can:','["Lower standards", "Encourage better performance", "Avoid them", "Reduce effort"]'::jsonb,1,'Motivation boosts output.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.B',3,'Praise and a sense of achievement from doing a good job are:','["Extrinsic rewards", "Taxes", "Intrinsic rewards", "Penalties"]'::jsonb,2,'Intrinsic rewards come from within.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.B',4,'A bonus or a raise is an example of an:','["Intrinsic reward", "Warning", "Policy", "Extrinsic reward"]'::jsonb,3,'Extrinsic rewards are external.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.C',3,'An employee feels paid less than a coworker doing the same job. The manager should:','["Review the pay fairly and discuss the concern", "Hide pay data", "Fire the employee", "Ignore it"]'::jsonb,0,'Equity concerns need attention.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.C',4,'Perceived inequity can lead employees to:','["Ignore pay", "Lower their effort or leave", "Increase loyalty", "Work harder always"]'::jsonb,1,'Unfairness harms motivation.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.D',3,'Expectancy Theory says people are motivated when they believe effort leads to:','["Punishment", "Less work", "Performance and valued rewards", "Boredom"]'::jsonb,2,'Effort, performance, and reward must link.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.D',4,'According to Expectancy Theory, an employee will work harder when:','["Rewards are random", "Rewards are unwanted", "Goals are impossible", "They believe effort will be rewarded"]'::jsonb,3,'Expectancy links effort to reward.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.E',3,'Clear goals and fair rewards usually make employees:','["More motivated", "Less engaged", "Less productive", "Unclear"]'::jsonb,0,'Goals and rewards motivate.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.E',4,'A goal that is specific and measurable helps because it:','["Cannot be tracked", "Shows employees exactly what success means", "Is vague", "Has no deadline"]'::jsonb,1,'Specific goals guide effort.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.F',3,'Compared with a manager, a leader mainly focuses on:','["Filing forms", "Balancing books", "Inspiring people toward a vision", "Counting inventory"]'::jsonb,2,'Leaders inspire.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.F',4,'A manager is typically responsible for:','["Only vision", "Only motivation", "Only charisma", "Planning, organizing, and controlling work"]'::jsonb,3,'Managers keep operations running.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.G',3,'A leader who guides a team toward a goal plays the role of:','["Direction setter", "Critic", "Bystander", "Observer only"]'::jsonb,0,'Leaders set direction.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.G',4,'One role of a leader is to:','["Hide information", "Inspire trust and encourage others", "Avoid decisions", "Blame the team"]'::jsonb,1,'Trust fuels teams.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.H',3,'Honesty, vision, and good communication are traits of an:','["Poor planner", "Ineffective leader", "Effective leader", "Lazy worker"]'::jsonb,2,'Traits support leadership.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.H',4,'Which trait helps a leader earn respect?','["Inconsistency", "Favoritism", "Secrecy", "Integrity"]'::jsonb,3,'Integrity builds credibility.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.I',3,'A leader who makes all decisions alone uses the:','["Autocratic style", "Democratic style", "Team style", "Laissez-faire style"]'::jsonb,0,'Autocratic leaders decide alone.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.I',4,'A leader who asks the team to vote on a decision uses the:','["Strict style", "Democratic style", "Laissez-faire style", "Autocratic style"]'::jsonb,1,'Democratic leaders involve others.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.J',3,'In a crisis requiring fast action, which style may fit best?','["Democratic", "Laissez-faire", "Autocratic", "None"]'::jsonb,2,'Emergencies need quick decisions.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.J',4,'A leader managing a team of highly skilled experts may choose a:','["No leadership", "Autocratic order", "Strict control", "Laissez-faire style that allows independence"]'::jsonb,3,'Experts need freedom.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.K',3,'Sending a message, the receiver decoding it, and feedback make up the:','["Communication process", "Production line", "Payroll cycle", "Hiring plan"]'::jsonb,0,'Communication has sender, message, receiver, and feedback.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.K',4,'In the management communication process, feedback shows whether the:','["Boss is present", "Message was understood", "Pay is fair", "Room is clean"]'::jsonb,1,'Feedback closes the loop.','original'),
