('127.247.d.5.L',4,'Managers should recognize that perception can cause:','["No reactions", "Identical views", "Equal feelings", "Messages to be understood differently"]'::jsonb,3,'Perception varies.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.M',3,'Noise, such as a loud machine, can interfere with:','["The communication process", "Hiring", "Inventory", "Payroll"]'::jsonb,0,'Noise blocks messages.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.M',4,'A manager sends a vague memo and employees ask many questions. The likely breakdown is in the:','["Office size", "Message clarity", "Employee pay", "Break time"]'::jsonb,1,'Unclear messages cause confusion.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.N',3,'An official memo from the CEO is an example of:','["Gossip", "Informal communication", "Formal communication", "Rumor"]'::jsonb,2,'Formal channels follow structure.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.N',4,'Conversation at lunch about company news is typically:','["A report", "Formal communication", "A policy", "Informal communication"]'::jsonb,3,'Informal communication flows through social ties.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.O',3,'A manager holds regular team meetings and invites questions to:','["Improve communication", "Lower morale", "Cut staff", "Waste time"]'::jsonb,0,'Regular exchange helps.','original'),
('127.247.d.5.O',4,'To improve communication, a company can:','["Restrict information", "Encourage open feedback and use clear channels", "Ignore questions", "Hide updates"]'::jsonb,1,'Open channels help.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.A',3,'Setting standards, measuring performance, and correcting deviations is the:','["Hiring process", "Branding process", "Control process", "Planning process"]'::jsonb,2,'Control compares to standards.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.A',4,'The first step in the control process is to:','["Skip measurement", "Ignore results", "Take corrective action", "Establish performance standards"]'::jsonb,3,'Standards come first.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.B',3,'Which is a primary control method?','["Budgets", "Wishes", "Rumors", "Gossip"]'::jsonb,0,'Budgets control spending.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.B',4,'Reviewing financial statements to check performance is a form of:','["Marketing", "Financial control", "Delegation", "Branding"]'::jsonb,1,'Financial control monitors money.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.C',3,'Quality control helps a business by:','["Raising errors", "Slowing hiring", "Reducing defects and returns", "Increasing waste"]'::jsonb,2,'Quality control catches defects.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.C',4,'A factory that inspects products before shipping practices:','["Competition", "Recruiting", "Advertising", "Quality control"]'::jsonb,3,'Inspection ensures quality.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.D',3,'Accurate sales reports help managers make better:','["Decisions", "Rumors", "Excuses", "Errors"]'::jsonb,0,'Information supports decisions.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.D',4,'Management information systems are strategically important because they:','["Slow reports", "Supply timely data for decisions", "Replace employees", "Add confusion"]'::jsonb,1,'Timely data guides strategy.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.E',3,'When departments share sales data, the company can:','["Delay orders", "Lose accuracy", "Coordinate better", "Duplicate work"]'::jsonb,2,'Sharing aligns work.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.E',4,'Gathering information is not useful unless it is:','["Incomplete", "Outdated", "Locked away", "Shared with people who can act on it"]'::jsonb,3,'Information must reach users.','original'),
