('127.247.d.6.I',4,'A restaurant measures service quality by tracking:','["Wall color", "Fork weight", "Wait times and customer satisfaction", "Parking size"]'::jsonb,2,'Service quality is customer-centered.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.J',3,'The Baldrige National Quality Award recognizes organizations for:','["Large size", "Low prices", "Old age", "Performance excellence"]'::jsonb,3,'The Baldrige honors excellence.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.J',4,'The Baldrige Award is given by:','["The United States government", "A newspaper", "A private club", "A foreign agency"]'::jsonb,0,'It is a U.S. presidential-level award program.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.K',3,'The Deming Award was created in:','["Brazil", "Japan", "France", "Canada"]'::jsonb,1,'Japan established the Deming Prize.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.K',4,'The Deming Award is named for a quality expert who:','["Invented the telephone", "Founded a retailer", "Taught statistical quality control to Japanese industry", "Wrote tax law"]'::jsonb,2,'W. Edwards Deming promoted quality methods.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.L',3,'To critique a recent Baldrige winner, a student should:','["Guess", "Skip research", "Copy the winner''s ad", "Use criteria and evidence from reliable reports"]'::jsonb,3,'Critiques need evidence.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.L',4,'A fair critique of a Baldrige recipient examines:','["Its results against the award criteria", "Its logo", "Its slogan", "Its building color"]'::jsonb,0,'Criteria drive the evaluation.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.M',3,'Researching a past Deming winner requires:','["Rumors", "Appropriate criteria and credible sources", "No sources", "Guesses"]'::jsonb,1,'Reliable research is essential.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.M',4,'When critiquing a Deming recipient, compare its practices to:','["A rumor", "A competitor''s ads", "The award''s quality standards", "A movie"]'::jsonb,2,'Use the stated standards.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.N',3,'Total Quality Management means:','["Cutting prices only", "Ignoring defects", "Inspecting once a year", "Continuously improving quality in every part of the organization"]'::jsonb,3,'TQM involves everyone.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.N',4,'A key idea of TQM is that:','["Customer satisfaction drives improvement", "Costs never matter", "Managers alone improve quality", "Inspection ends quality work"]'::jsonb,0,'TQM is customer-focused.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.O',3,'Operations that provide help, such as repairs or haircuts, are:','["Manufacturing operations", "Service operations", "Farming operations", "Mining operations"]'::jsonb,1,'Services provide intangible help.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.O',4,'Unlike a product, a service is usually:','["Mass-produced and shelved", "Stored in a warehouse", "Intangible and produced as it is delivered", "Sold by weight"]'::jsonb,2,'Services are consumed as provided.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.P',3,'A survey that asks customers to rate their experience is a:','["Contract", "Tax form", "Resume", "Customer satisfaction instrument"]'::jsonb,3,'Surveys measure satisfaction.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.P',4,'A good satisfaction survey includes:','["Clear questions and a rating scale", "Only open comments", "No questions", "Confusing questions"]'::jsonb,0,'Clear scales aid analysis.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.Q',3,'Studying how a factory turns materials into finished goods is analyzing:','["Retail operations", "Manufacturing operations", "Hotel operations", "Banking operations"]'::jsonb,1,'Manufacturing converts inputs to products.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.Q',4,'A manager who studies a production line to find delays is analyzing:','["Logos", "Break rooms", "Operations efficiency", "Dress codes"]'::jsonb,2,'Analysis finds waste.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.R',3,'The goods a store holds for sale are its:','["Payroll", "Mortgage", "Revenue", "Inventory"]'::jsonb,3,'Inventory is stock on hand.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.R',4,'Raw materials, work in process, and finished goods are all kinds of:','["Inventory", "Debts", "Wages", "Taxes"]'::jsonb,0,'Inventory has several stages.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.S',3,'Too much inventory ties up money in:','["Advertising", "Unsold goods", "Wages", "Rent only"]'::jsonb,1,'Excess stock locks up cash.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.S',4,'Controlling inventory is fiscally important because it:','["Lowers sales", "Raises waste", "Reduces storage costs and prevents shortages", "Increases theft"]'::jsonb,2,'Balanced inventory saves money.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.A',3,'Believing that all workers of one group behave alike is a:','["Fact", "Law", "Policy", "Stereotype"]'::jsonb,3,'Stereotypes overgeneralize.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.A',4,'Recognizing your own biases helps you:','["Make fairer decisions", "Hide mistakes", "Judge others faster", "Avoid change"]'::jsonb,0,'Awareness reduces bias.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.B',3,'Listening before responding to a coworker''s concern is an effective:','["Competition", "Interpersonal skill", "Accounting rule", "Delay tactic"]'::jsonb,1,'Good interpersonal skills include listening.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.B',4,'Which action shows strong interpersonal skills in a disagreement?','["Raising your voice", "Blaming others", "Staying calm and respectful", "Walking away"]'::jsonb,2,'Respect keeps conversations productive.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.C',3,'Planning an activity so a new team learns to trust one another is:','["Auditing", "Discipline", "Hiring", "Team building"]'::jsonb,3,'Team building builds trust.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.C',4,'An effective team-building skill is:','["Clarifying roles and sharing credit", "Blaming", "Hoarding tasks", "Ignoring input"]'::jsonb,0,'Shared credit builds cohesion.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.D',3,'Serving as a club officer is an example of:','["An accounting task", "A leadership activity", "A shipping task", "A waiting activity"]'::jsonb,1,'Officers lead.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.D',4,'Leading a group project gives a student practice in:','["Working alone", "Avoiding work", "Organizing others and meeting goals", "Following only"]'::jsonb,2,'Leadership builds skills.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.E',3,'Job shadowing a manager is a:','["Layoff", "Disciplinary action", "Payroll task", "Career development activity"]'::jsonb,3,'Shadowing explores careers.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.E',4,'A career development activity that builds skills for advancement is:','["Attending a management workshop", "Skipping class", "Avoiding training", "Ignoring feedback"]'::jsonb,0,'Workshops build skills.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.F',3,'Listing what you do well and what you need to improve is a:','["Resume", "Self-assessment", "Budget", "Invoice"]'::jsonb,1,'Self-assessment finds strengths and weaknesses.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.F',4,'Knowing your weaknesses allows you to:','["Ignore growth", "Blame others", "Plan for improvement", "Hide them forever"]'::jsonb,2,'Awareness leads to growth.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.G',3,'Arriving on time, being honest, and showing initiative help foster:','["Layoffs", "Conflicts", "Delays", "Career advancement"]'::jsonb,3,'Good traits help promotion.','original'),
('127.247.d.7.G',4,'Which trait most helps an employee earn a promotion?','["Dependability", "Gossip", "Carelessness", "Lateness"]'::jsonb,0,'Dependability gains trust.','original'),
('127.247.d.8.A',3,'Listing the people, money, and equipment a project needs is part of:','["Closing a project", "Initiating a project", "Marketing", "Monitoring only"]'::jsonb,1,'Initiation identifies resources.','original'),
('127.247.d.8.A',4,'Before a project starts, a manager should identify:','["The final results", "The next project", "The resources needed and the project''s purpose", "The retirement plan"]'::jsonb,2,'Initiation defines scope.','original'),
('127.247.d.8.B',3,'A written project plan lists tasks, deadlines, and:','["Menus", "Rumors", "Songs", "Responsible people"]'::jsonb,3,'Plans assign ownership.','original'),
('127.247.d.8.B',4,'A project plan helps a team by:','["Showing who does what and by when", "Hiding tasks", "Avoiding roles", "Removing deadlines"]'::jsonb,0,'Clarity aids execution.','original'),
('127.247.d.8.C',3,'Carrying out the tasks in the plan is:','["Planning", "Executing the project", "Closing", "Initiating"]'::jsonb,1,'Execution does the work.','original'),
('127.247.d.8.C',4,'During execution, the team should:','["Rewrite the goal", "Stop reporting", "Complete assigned tasks and communicate progress", "Wait"]'::jsonb,2,'Execution needs updates.','original'),
('127.247.d.8.D',3,'Comparing progress with the schedule and budget is:','["Initiating", "Closing", "Brainstorming", "Monitoring and controlling"]'::jsonb,3,'Monitoring keeps projects on track.','original'),
('127.247.d.8.D',4,'If costs exceed the budget, a manager should:','["Investigate the cause and adjust", "Add costs", "Hide the numbers", "Ignore it"]'::jsonb,0,'Control takes corrective action.','original'),
('127.247.d.8.E',3,'Delivering the final product and reviewing lessons learned is:','["Delaying a project", "Closing a project", "Initiating a project", "Planning a project"]'::jsonb,1,'Closing finalizes work.','original'),
('127.247.d.8.E',4,'At project closing, a team should:','["Ignore reviews", "Delete all records", "Document results and lessons learned", "Start over"]'::jsonb,2,'Closure captures knowledge.','original'),
('127.247.d.6.F',5,'A plant raises output 8% while holding labor hours constant. Which management result does this best show?','["Lower quality control", "A reduced span of control", "Greater turnover", "Higher productivity that supports growth"]'::jsonb,3,'More output from the same inputs is productivity.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
